      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened on January 13, 1879, and remained in service until 1954, after which the town became a quiet farming community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/inland_nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nestled in the fertile Republican River valley, Inland's loess soil supports corn, soybeans, and cattle, typical of south‑central Nebraska's farming belt.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/inland_nebraska",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The one‑room Inland School, built in 1920, was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2002, highlighting the town's farm‑heritage education.",
